-- title:
--   Kernel of reduction on A∩ℚ is generated by q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose vanishing locus is exactly the maximal ideal of the local ring $A$: for every $c \in A$, $\mathrm{red}(c) = 0$ if and only if $c$ lies in `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A`. Write $A_0 :=$ `coeffSubring A ⊥` for the subring $A \cap \mathbb{Q}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the intersection of $A$ with the bottom intermediate field $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let `redRestrict red ⊥` be the composite of the inclusion $A_0 \hookrightarrow A$ with $\mathrm{red}$. Then for every $c \in A_0$ the assertion $\mathrm{red}(c) = 0$ is equivalent to the existence of $d \in A_0$ with $c = q\,d$, where $q$ denotes the image of the natural number $q$ under the canonical map $\mathbb{N} \to A_0$. In other words, the kernel of the restricted reduction map on $A \cap \mathbb{Q}$ is the principal ideal generated by $q$.
--
--   This is the concrete identification $A \cap \mathbb{Q} = \mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$ with maximal ideal $(q)$, in the form needed to supply a uniformiser at the base field $\mathbb{Q}$: it certifies that $\varpi := q$ generates the kernel of the reduction restricted to the coefficient ring over $\mathbb{Q}$, so ramification index $e_{\mathbb{Q}} = 1$. It is used in the construction of admissible representatives in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.exists_goodRep_admissible_smul_single_sub_self_of_eq_zero_or_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.exists_goodRep_admissible_smul_single_sub_self_of_eq_zero_or_eq), where crossing presentations for the node ring must be instantiated over the base field $\mathbb{Q}$.
